Z||000000||mikeyd612||09-06-2001||10:16 PM||||I have an 87' se 4 cylinder. I have now had the head gasket replaced, the head machined, egr valve replaced, and tps sensor replaced. The car, when hot and intermitenly, stumbles, almost like it's missing, sometimes it will stall on its own shortly after starting, or if I get the chance to shift into drive before stalling, the shift into drive usually drops the power enough to stall it. It only happens after it's hot (210 degrees), and is just getting started up after being stopped for a while. In addition to replacing the parts listed above, the mechanic who is now looking at it has tested a new map sensor, used ecm, used but good ignition coils, vacumn hoses, cleaned the grounds, and checked engine wiring for shorts. Any additional info someone might have would be helpful.||||reg||5
